// The Swift-facing module for the Rust audio engine's C ABI, off Apple.
//
// On Apple platforms the engine arrives as an XCFramework, which carries its
// own copy of this map (see tools/build-audio-xcframework.sh). An XCFramework
// is built by `xcodebuild -create-xcframework` and cannot exist anywhere else,
// so Windows and Linux need their own way to see the same header — otherwise
// the desktop build fails at manifest load, before a line is compiled.
//
// Same module name and same header as the Apple side, deliberately: it means
// `import MozzAudioFFI` in Sources/MozzAudioEngine is one import satisfied
// differently per host, not two spellings that can drift apart.
//
// Headers only. The library itself is `libmozz_audio_ffi.a` (or
// `mozz_audio_ffi.lib`), named by MozzAudioEngine's linkerSettings and found
// through a search path the build passes in — the same shape the package
// already uses for SQLite.
module MozzAudioFFI {
    header "../include/mozz_audio.h"
    export *
}
